<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-regional-manager-emea-data-center-capacity-delivery-london-451996> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-26T04:45:30+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/anthropic/regional-manager-emea-data-center-capacity-delivery-london-451996> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "d5db13b92c94b8103c9d7ef706f6685cc6e464774a1d2b5a8245abcdcce6bd73" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-26T01:41:29+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-26T04:45:30+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "regional-manager-emea-data-center-capacity-delivery-london-451996" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2> <p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p>Training and serving frontier AI models requires data center capacity at a scale and pace that conventional delivery models were not built for. Anthropic's Data Center Capacity Delivery team embeds with developers, general contractors, and third-party partners to take leased and partnered sites from deal close through floor access and operational handover as fast as they can safely be built.</p><p>As a Regional Manager, you'll own delivery across a regional portfolio of active and upcoming projects. You'll build and lead the team of Senior Delivery Managers and third-party partners who sit on those sites, set the standards they execute to, and step in yourself where a project needs it. You are the executive-level interface to our developer partners in the region and the intake point for projects handed over from our transaction team.</p><p>This is a highly cross-functional role: you'll work daily with our transaction, design engineering, facility operations and commissioning, deployment, and safety teams, and with developers, GCs, and owner's-representative firms on the ground.</p><h2><strong>MOC (Mission + Outcomes + Competencies)</strong></h2><h3><strong>Mission</strong></h3><p>Deliver the region’s data center projects to floor access as fast as they can safely be built.</p><h3><strong>Outcomes</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Every active project in the region delivered against early-floor-access and floor-access milestones.</p></li><li><p>Senior Delivery Manager team hired and led; owner’s-rep partners contracted and managed.</p></li><li><p>Delivery standards (schedule, quality, change control, reporting) enforced across the portfolio.</p></li><li><p>Executive reporting on progress vs plan and regional capacity projections in place.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Competencies</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Senior owner- or GC-side mission-critical delivery leadership.</p></li><li><p>Builds and leads multi-project teams.</p></li><li><p>Executive-level developer and GC relationship management.</p></li><li><p>Leads on site through presence; owns outcomes where no process exists.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Lead. This is a role where leadership trumps management and process. You are expected to be on the region's sites enough to shape the culture, approach, and aggressiveness that define the extended teams there — across the portfolio, not one project — and to impact outcomes in a favorable manner.</p></li><li><p>Be a force multiplier. Hire, develop, empower, and lead the Senior Delivery Managers on those sites, and raise the skillset developers, contractors, owner's-rep partners, and key trades bring to every project in the region; plan resourcing and headcount as the portfolio grows.</p></li><li><p>Own portfolio execution for the region — schedule, quality, and safety outcomes on every active project, measured against early-floor-access and floor-access milestones. You are empowered and have autonomy to own this regions record of performance.</p></li><li><p>Drive ownership and influence both inside and outside contractual structures: select, scope, contract, and manage owner's-rep and project-management partners; where contracts, incentives, or culture get in the way of speed, change them, and replace partners when performance or culture slips</p></li><li><p>Set and enforce delivery standards across projects — integrated schedule, quality requirements, change control, reporting, and tools — and validate that they are met</p></li><li><p>Identify blockers early and clear them across developer, GC, and trade layers; step in on site where a project needs it</p></li></ul><h2><strong>You may be a good fit if you</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Have [10+] years delivering data center or other mission-critical construction, including several as the owner's or GC's senior leader on a project campus</p></li><li><p>Have led a multi-project portfolio and built the team that delivered it</p></li><li><p>Know the end-to-end development process — entitlements and permitting, design, long-lead equipment, construction, commissioning, and handover — well enough to direct partners rather than take their word for it</p></li><li><p>Have managed developer, GC, and third-party relationships at the executive level and can move them from arm's-length contract administration to shared urgency</p></li><li><p>Lead through presence: you expect to be on site most of the time and to set the pace and culture of extended teams you don't directly employ</p></li><li><p>Communicate clearly with technical and non-specialist stakeholders and hold a position when challenged</p></li><li><p>Are comfortable with ambiguity and with owning outcomes where no process exists yet</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Strong candidates may also have</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Hyperscale data center delivery experience on the owner, developer, or GC side</p></li><li><p>Experience with the UK and continental European market — its contractors, permitting regimes, and contractual norms</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with lease, construction, and development contract structures and how to align their incentives around speed</p></li></ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p>The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&nbsp;</p> <p>For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.</p></div><div class=\"title\">Annual Salary:</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>£1</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>£1 GBP</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><h2><strong>Logistics</strong></h2> <p><strong>Minimum education: </strong>Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience</p> <p><strong>Required field of study:&nbsp;</strong>A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience</p> <p><strong>Minimum years of experience: </strong>Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position</p> <p><strong>Location-based hybrid policy:</strong> Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.</p> <p><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Visa sponsorship:</strong>&nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren't able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.</p> <p><strong>We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.</strong> Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you're interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we're building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.<br><br><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Your safety matters to us.</strong> To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you ----- addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you're ever unsure about a communication, don't click any links—visit&nbsp;<u data-stringify-type=\"underline\"><a class=\"c-link c-link--underline\" href=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"http://anthropic.com/careers\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\" data-remove-tab-index=\"true\">anthropic.com/careers</a></u>&nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.</p> <h2><strong>How we're different</strong></h2> <p>We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We're an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.</p> <p>The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.</p> <h2><strong>Come work with us!</strong></h2> <p>Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. <strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Guidance on Candidates' AI Usage:</strong>&nbsp;Learn about&nbsp;<a class=\"c-link\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\">our policy</a> for using AI in our application process.</p></div> Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-anthropic ;
    schema:identifier "arbeitnow-regional-manager-emea-data-center-capacity-delivery-london-451996" ;
    schema:jobLocation [ a schema:Place ;
            schema:name "London" ] ;
    schema:title "Regional Manager EMEA, Data Center Capacity Delivery" ;
    schema:url <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/anthropic/regional-manager-emea-data-center-capacity-delivery-london-451996> .

<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-remote-lead-data-platform-engineer-98007> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-26T04:45:30+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/akersystems/remote-lead-data-platform-engineer-98007> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "c360bf0c87ce8679046090ba0f082f5f52bbbc9e10c33a3dde3f8b348a50a142" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-25T17:36:20+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-26T04:45:30+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "remote-lead-data-platform-engineer-98007" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Aker Systems was founded in 2017 by a team of experienced technology professionals who recognised an opportunity to provide highly secure enterprise data platforms to large organisations.&nbsp; We build and operate ground-breaking, ultra-secure, high performance, cloud-based data infrastructure for the enterprise. Our proprietary technology solutions drive performance and reduce costs while helping our clients to improve the management and sharing of data across their organisations.</p> <p>In 2024, Aker Systems won the Breakthrough Culture Awards highlighting growth companies putting culture first. In 2020 Aker Systems was recognised as a ‘One to Watch’ on the Sunday Times Tech Track.&nbsp; The Company was also recognised at the Thames Valley Tech Awards 2020; winning the Thames Valley Tech Company of the year, the Emerging Tech Company and High Growth Tech Business categories.&nbsp; We encourage people of all different backgrounds and identities to apply.&nbsp; We are committed to maintaining an inclusive, and supportive place for you to do your very best work.</p></div><p>Location</p> <p>UK / Remote</p> <p>Clearance</p> <p>Depending on the client assignment, UK Government Security Check (SC) clearance may be required. Where SC clearance is required, candidates who do not currently hold clearance may be supported through the application process, subject to eligibility requirements, including having lived and worked in the UK for a minimum of 5 years.</p> <p>The Role</p> <p>We are looking for a Lead Data Platform Engineer to provide hands-on technical leadership in designing, building and evolving secure, scalable and reliable data platforms for clients across the public sector and utilities.</p> <p>You will work across cloud-native and distributed data platforms, helping engineering teams build reliable platform capabilities that support batch, real-time streaming, analytical and operational workloads.</p> <p>The role combines hands-on engineering with technical leadership. You will contribute to platform architecture and design decisions, establish engineering standards, solve complex technical challenges and work closely with architects, engineers and client stakeholders.</p> <p>Strong experience with cloud platforms, distributed systems and data platform engineering is essential.</p> <p>Key Responsibilities</p> <ul> <li>Lead the design, development and evolution of secure, scalable data platform services and components.</li> <li>Design and implement platform capabilities supporting batch, real-time streaming and hybrid workloads.</li> <li>Build and optimise distributed data services using technologies such as Kafka, Kinesis, Spark, Flink or equivalent.</li> <li>Contribute to platform architecture and technical design decisions, balancing scalability, security, performance and maintainability.</li> <li>Work closely with architects and engineers to establish reusable platform patterns, standards and engineering practices.</li> <li>Develop cloud-native data platform capabilities using AWS and/or Azure.</li> <li>Support high availability, fault tolerance, resilience and low-latency performance across platform services.</li> <li>Establish and maintain approaches to data modelling, schema management, data quality and data integrity.</li> <li>Drive engineering best practices including CI/CD, automated testing, TDD, observability and Infrastructure as Code.</li> <li>Support platform monitoring, troubleshooting, performance optimisation and root cause analysis.</li> <li>Contribute to resilience, disaster recovery and operational readiness activities.</li> <li>Work with DevOps and Platform Engineering teams to improve deployment and operational processes.</li> <li>Support technical discovery and solution design with client stakeholders.</li> <li>Provide technical guidance, mentoring and support to Senior Data and Platform Engineers.</li> <li>Identify technical risks, dependencies and opportunities for continuous improvement.</li> </ul> <p>Essential Technical Skills &amp; Experience</p> <ul> <li>Strong commercial experience in Data Platform Engineering, Data Engineering, Software Engineering or a similar technical discipline, with experience operating at Lead level.</li> <li>Experience designing and building cloud-native, distributed data platforms.</li> <li>Strong experience with Java and/or Python or equivalent modern programming languages.</li> <li>Experience with streaming and event-driven architectures, including Kafka, Kinesis or equivalent.</li> <li>Experience with large-scale data processing technologies such as Spark, Flink, Kafka Streams or equivalent.</li> <li>Strong experience working with AWS and/or Azure cloud environments.</li> <li>Experience with AWS services such as S3, Lambda, Glue, RDS, Athena, EC2 and IAM is desirable.</li> <li>Strong understanding of data pipeline architecture, orchestration and optimisation.</li> <li>Experience with relational and NoSQL databases, including data modelling and performance tuning.</li> <li>Experience implementing CI/CD, automated testing, observability and platform reliability practices.</li> <li>Strong understanding of DevOps and Infrastructure as Code.</li> <li>Experience with GitHub/GitLab or equivalent source control platforms.</li> <li>Experience working in Agile and/or DevOps environments.</li> <li>Desirable: Terraform, Docker, Kubernetes, Ansible, Packer, Elasticsearch/OpenSearch, Jenkins, GitLab CI, Python, Bash or Linux.</li> <li>Experience working within public sector, utilities or other regulated environments is advantageous.</li> </ul> <p>Technical Leadership</p> <p>As a Lead Data Platform Engineer, you will provide technical leadership within delivery teams and platform engineering activities.</p> <p>You will:</p> <ul> <li>Lead the technical delivery of data platform capabilities and services.</li> <li>Contribute to platform architecture, technical design and technology decisions.</li> <li>Establish reusable engineering patterns and promote consistent technical standards.</li> <li>Support and mentor Senior Data and Platform Engineers.</li> <li>Work closely with architects, developers, DevOps and client stakeholders.</li> <li>Identify technical debt, platform risks and opportunities for improvement.</li> <li>Promote secure, scalable, observable and maintainable engineering practices.</li> <li>Support teams in balancing technical quality with delivery timelines and client outcomes.</li> <li>Contribute to platform resilience, operational readiness and continuous improvement.</li> </ul> <p>Experience &amp; Qualifications</p> <p>A Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Data Engineering or a related technical discipline is desirable.</p> <p>You should have 5+ years of relevant professional experience across Data Engineering, Software Engineering, Platform Engineering or a similar technical discipline.</p> <p>For a Lead-level appointment, you should demonstrate experience taking ownership of complex platform engineering solutions, technical decisions and mentoring or guiding other engineers.</p> <p>Security Clearance</p> <p>Where required by the client assignment, UK Government Security Check (SC) clearance may be required.</p> <p>Candidates who do not currently hold SC clearance may be supported through the clearance process, subject to eligibility requirements.</p> <p>About You</p> <p>You are a hands-on platform engineer who understands how to build reliable data infrastructure that works in production.</p> <p>You enjoy solving complex problems across cloud, distributed systems, streaming, data platforms and infrastructure, and can translate architectural requirements into practical engineering solutions.</p> <p>You are comfortable moving between hands-on development, technical design and stakeholder discussions, while helping other engineers improve their technical capability.</p> <p>You care about reliability, scalability, security, observability and maintainability, not simply getting a platform into production.</p> <p>Experience working within public sector, utilities or other complex and regulated environments would be highly advantageous.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Aker Systems Attributes</span></p> <p>At Aker we work as a team; we are collaborative, hardworking, open, and delivery obsessed. There is no blame culture here: try things, and take responsibility for the outcomes. You are always part of the wider Aker. We help our colleagues and take pride in successfully achieving difficult tasks. We run towards problems and help to solve them. Communicate always, do so accurately and in a timely fashion.</p> <p>In return, we offer a competitive salary, 25 days holiday plus bank holidays, company paid medical insurance and life assurance, pension scheme, annual training allowance, wellbeing allowance, virtual GP, Employee Assistance plan and more.</p> <p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Equal Opportunities</span></p> <p>Aker Systems fosters a diverse environment that encourages openness in its communications and is committed to providing equal employment opportunity for all people regardless of race, religion, gender or sexual orientation, age, marital status, national origin, citizenship status, disability, veteran status or other personal characteristics. We embrace differences of opinion and diversity because they help challenge us and find new groundbreaking technical solutions.</p></div> Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-akersystems ;
